# Data fetching in apps/web

Document routes put **real data in the first HTML**. Loaders `fetchQuery` the same `*Query()` factories, `dehydrate`, and wrap the page in `HydrationBoundary`. The page `useQuery` reads that cache. Skeletons are a fallback when the cache is empty.

Do not fetch in `useEffect`. Every non-docs API call waits **200–2000ms** and fails **~10%** of the time — keep round trips low. Do not invent URLs; use the Home Garden API skill. Do not disable the API delay/error plugins.

## Ownership

```
Document page (/gardens): loader fetchQuery + dehydrate → HydrationBoundary → page useQuery/useMutation → organism props
MPA page (/my-garden): static stub. No loader or query until the feature is implemented
```

- Put keys, `queryOptions`, and mutation fns in `app/queries/*`.
- Call `useQuery` / `useMutation` only in **pages**. Document routes also own the matching `loader`.
- Pass results into organisms. Never `useQuery` in atoms, molecules, or templates.
- Use `api()` from `app/lib/api.ts` only. Name wrappers `<httpMethod><Resource>` (`getGardens`, `postGarden`). `queryOptions` factories stay `*Query`.

## QueryClient and round trips

Browser singleton via `getQueryClient()`. New client on the server (loader and SSR). Never share a server client across requests.

Loader QueryClient: `retry: false`. Browser: `staleTime` 60s, `retry: 2`. Tests: **`retry: false`**. Hydration must not refetch the list within `staleTime`.

List queries may set `refetchInterval` for quiet freshness (`GARDENS_REFETCH_INTERVAL_MS` on `/gardens`). Turn it off in tests. `refetchIntervalInBackground: false`. Polling is how other tabs see creates; do not `invalidateQueries` the list after local `setQueryData`.

Dehydrate **success and error** queries. Do not redact errors. Serialize `ApiError` as `{ name, message, status }` so loader data round-trips.

Create garden: `setQueryData` on `gardenKeys.list()` with the created entity. Do not `invalidateQueries` the list just to refresh — that refetches the slow API and fights SSR plus optimistic rows.

Use one list call for a list. Start independent requests together (`useQueries`) when the id is already in the URL. Do not fetch per row, waterfall `queryFn`s, or set `staleTime: 0`.

## Agent do / don't

**Do**

- Prefetch `/gardens` in a server `loader` with `fetchQuery(gardensQuery())`, `dehydrateQueryState`, and `HydrationBoundary`
- Use `useQuery(gardensQuery())` on the gardens page to read that cache
- Use `refetchInterval` on list queries when another session should see new rows without a reload
- Keep `/my-garden` a static stub until the feature is implemented
- Name every `api()` wrapper `<httpMethod><Resource>`

**Don't**

- `useEffect` + `fetch` / axios
- `useQuery` below the page layer, or on `/my-garden`
- Client-only first paint for a document route (skeleton while the list could have been in the HTML)
- Fetch per row inside a list item

## Good / bad

```tsx
export async function loader() {
  const queryClient = makeQueryClient({ retry: false });
  try {
    await queryClient.fetchQuery(gardensQuery());
  } catch (error) {
    if (!(error instanceof Error)) throw error;
  }
  return { dehydratedState: dehydrateQueryState(queryClient) };
}

export default function GardensPage({
  loaderData,
}: {
  loaderData?: { dehydratedState: DehydratedState };
}) {
  return (
    <HydrationBoundary state={loaderData?.dehydratedState}>
      <AppShell>
        <GardensPanel />
      </AppShell>
    </HydrationBoundary>
  );
}

function GardensPanel() {
  const { data, isPending, isError, refetch } = useQuery(gardensQuery());
  if (isPending) return <GardenListSkeleton />;
  if (isError && !data) {
    return <ErrorAlert error="Couldn't load gardens" details="Please try again." onRetry={() => refetch()} />;
  }
  return <GardenList gardens={data} />;
}
```

```tsx
// Bad — useEffect fetch; per-row query; no document loader
function GardenRow({ garden }: { garden: Garden }) {
  const plants = useQuery(plantsByGardenQuery(garden.gardenId));
  return <td>{plants.data?.length}</td>;
}
```
